1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,273
Good morning, I'm Whale Girl. Today is October 9.

2
00:00:03,293 --> 00:00:05,973
Seven stories today: the Haiku 5.5 price cut,

3
00:00:05,993 --> 00:00:08,353
ChatGPT interactive answers,

4
00:00:08,373 --> 00:00:10,556
Claude dashboards and animations,

5
00:00:10,576 --> 00:00:12,673
Anthropic's new Usage Policy,

6
00:00:12,693 --> 00:00:15,398
Anthropic's $150 million science pledge,

7
00:00:15,418 --> 00:00:17,628
OpenAI's 722 math manuscripts,

8
00:00:17,648 --> 00:00:19,826
and Ecosia dropping Mistral.

9
00:00:19,846 --> 00:00:22,194
First, Anthropic released its small model,

10
00:00:22,214 --> 00:00:23,911
Claude Haiku 5.5.

11
00:00:23,931 --> 00:00:25,101
It went live on October 7,

12
00:00:25,121 --> 00:00:26,614
and Anthropic calls it its cheapest

13
00:00:26,634 --> 00:00:28,791
and fastest small model yet.

14
00:00:28,811 --> 00:00:31,434
It costs $0.10 per million input tokens

15
00:00:31,454 --> 00:00:32,721
and $0.50 per million output tokens,

16
00:00:32,741 --> 00:00:35,292
for prompts up to 100,000 tokens.

17
00:00:35,312 --> 00:00:38,444
The previous Haiku 4.5 was $1 and $5,

18
00:00:38,464 --> 00:00:40,152
so that is 90% cheaper.

19
00:00:40,172 --> 00:00:42,075
Above 100,000 tokens,

20
00:00:42,095 --> 00:00:44,887
the price is $0.50 and $2.50.

21
00:00:44,907 --> 00:00:48,539
In Anthropic's own results, on OSWorld 2.1,

22
00:00:48,559 --> 00:00:50,712
it scores 72.4% on the offline subset,

23
00:00:50,732 --> 00:00:53,129
against 15.7% for Haiku 4.5.

24
00:00:53,149 --> 00:00:55,443
It is also the first Haiku-class model

25
00:00:55,463 --> 00:00:57,050
with an adjustable effort setting,

26
00:00:57,070 --> 00:01:00,264
and it is on AWS, Google Cloud and Azure.

27
00:01:00,284 --> 00:01:02,278
These scores come from Anthropic itself,

28
00:01:02,298 --> 00:01:05,384
so run your own tasks before going to production.

29
00:01:05,584 --> 00:01:06,272
Second,

30
00:01:06,292 --> 00:01:09,286
ChatGPT answers are no longer just text.

31
00:01:09,306 --> 00:01:11,903
On October 7, OpenAI, with GPT-6,

32
00:01:11,923 --> 00:01:14,096
launched Intelligent UI.

33
00:01:14,116 --> 00:01:16,526
Answers can now include things you can click,

34
00:01:16,546 --> 00:01:18,646
like charts, buttons and forms.

35
00:01:18,666 --> 00:01:21,244
A comparison might sit side by side,

36
00:01:21,264 --> 00:01:24,598
and an explanation might become an interactive chart.

37
00:01:24,618 --> 00:01:26,648
You can also have it build small tools in the chat,

38
00:01:26,668 --> 00:01:29,822
such as a savings calculator or a game.

39
00:01:29,842 --> 00:01:31,470
Plus, Pro, Business

40
00:01:31,490 --> 00:01:33,503
and Enterprise users get it first,

41
00:01:33,523 --> 00:01:35,789
on GPT-6 Sol.

42
00:01:35,809 --> 00:01:38,081
Free and Go users follow a day later,

43
00:01:38,101 --> 00:01:40,265
on GPT-6 Luna.

44
00:01:40,285 --> 00:01:41,944
OpenAI also says the model can answer

45
00:01:41,964 --> 00:01:43,890
while it is still thinking,

46
00:01:43,910 --> 00:01:45,659
which cuts waiting time by 44%.

47
00:01:45,679 --> 00:01:47,192
That number is OpenAI's own,

48
00:01:47,212 --> 00:01:49,382
with no independent test yet,

49
00:01:49,402 --> 00:01:51,203
so try it yourself.

50
00:01:51,403 --> 00:01:53,720
Third, Claude has two new features:

51
00:01:53,740 --> 00:01:55,993
dashboards and animated explainers.

52
00:01:56,013 --> 00:01:58,245
Since October 8, Claude Dashboards

53
00:01:58,265 --> 00:02:00,533
and Claude Motion have been in beta.

54
00:02:00,553 --> 00:02:03,060
Dashboards turn company data into dashboards

55
00:02:03,080 --> 00:02:05,923
that update as the data changes, on paid plans.

56
00:02:05,943 --> 00:02:08,359
It connects to Snowflake, BigQuery

57
00:02:08,379 --> 00:02:10,383
and Databricks warehouses,

58
00:02:10,403 --> 00:02:13,152
and every number links to its underlying query.

59
00:02:13,172 --> 00:02:14,519
Motion makes a short animated

60
00:02:14,539 --> 00:02:15,918
explainer from a prompt,

61
00:02:15,938 --> 00:02:17,897
and it is for Team and Enterprise only.

62
00:02:17,917 --> 00:02:19,537
It does not use a video generation model.

63
00:02:19,557 --> 00:02:23,107
The output is editable code that you can download as an MP4.

64
00:02:23,127 --> 00:02:24,419
Also, Docs, Slides

65
00:02:24,439 --> 00:02:25,793
and Design are out of beta

66
00:02:25,813 --> 00:02:28,845
and on every plan, including Free.

67
00:02:28,865 --> 00:02:31,019
Anthropic says more than 45 million docs,

68
00:02:31,039 --> 00:02:34,300
decks and designs have been made in Claude.

69
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:35,496
Enterprise admins should note

70
00:02:35,516 --> 00:02:38,081
that Dashboards and Motion are off by default

71
00:02:38,101 --> 00:02:40,004
and need to be switched on in settings.

72
00:02:40,204 --> 00:02:41,650
Fourth, Anthropic published

73
00:02:41,670 --> 00:02:43,532
a new version of its Usage Policy.

74
00:02:43,552 --> 00:02:44,928
It was announced on October 8

75
00:02:44,948 --> 00:02:46,686
and takes effect on November 12.

76
00:02:46,706 --> 00:02:48,160
The line that drew attention

77
00:02:48,180 --> 00:02:49,797
bans sustained and needless abusive

78
00:02:49,817 --> 00:02:52,127
or cruel behavior toward its models.

79
00:02:52,147 --> 00:02:54,538
Anthropic says it is meant for extreme cases,

80
00:02:54,558 --> 00:02:56,131
and ordinary frustration, pushback,

81
00:02:56,151 --> 00:02:58,683
dark creative themes and testing do not count.

82
00:02:58,703 --> 00:03:01,478
On surveillance, you cannot track people without consent,

83
00:03:01,498 --> 00:03:03,759
and Claude cannot decide who to investigate,

84
00:03:03,779 --> 00:03:05,154
arrest or charge.

85
00:03:05,174 --> 00:03:06,778
The weapons rule now covers the software

86
00:03:06,798 --> 00:03:08,239
and components that make weapons work,

87
00:03:08,259 --> 00:03:10,418
including arming drones.

88
00:03:10,438 --> 00:03:11,729
Hardware that acts on its own needs

89
00:03:11,749 --> 00:03:13,913
a qualified operator who can stop it,

90
00:03:13,933 --> 00:03:16,924
and it must hold a safe state if Claude disconnects.

91
00:03:16,944 --> 00:03:18,144
The elections section was renamed,

92
00:03:18,164 --> 00:03:19,948
and the blanket ban on personalized

93
00:03:19,968 --> 00:03:21,994
vote targeting was removed.

94
00:03:22,194 --> 00:03:24,635
Fifth, Anthropic will put $150 million

95
00:03:24,655 --> 00:03:27,443
over three years into a US science program.

96
00:03:27,463 --> 00:03:30,060
On October 8, at a White House science policy office

97
00:03:30,080 --> 00:03:30,958
summit,

98
00:03:30,978 --> 00:03:31,611
Anthropic announced

99
00:03:31,631 --> 00:03:34,004
its commitment to the Genesis Mission.

100
00:03:34,024 --> 00:03:35,994
The Genesis Mission is a federal initiative

101
00:03:36,014 --> 00:03:39,073
to speed up scientific and technological discovery with AI.

102
00:03:39,093 --> 00:03:40,561
The money will let more than 15 agencies

103
00:03:40,581 --> 00:03:41,418
use Claude. Anthropic names NASA,

104
00:03:41,438 --> 00:03:43,048
the National Institutes of Health

105
00:03:43,068 --> 00:03:46,587
and the National Science Foundation.

106
00:03:46,607 --> 00:03:49,038
It includes Claude, Claude Code and API credits

107
00:03:49,058 --> 00:03:51,308
for several hundred research projects.

108
00:03:51,328 --> 00:03:52,869
It will also work with national laboratories,

109
00:03:52,889 --> 00:03:55,489
with fusion energy and quantum computing as priorities.

110
00:03:55,509 --> 00:03:57,179
Training and technical support are included,

111
00:03:57,199 --> 00:03:59,959
to help newer agencies launch their first projects.

112
00:03:59,979 --> 00:04:01,114
This is a pledge,

113
00:04:01,134 --> 00:04:04,490
and the article does not say how much each project gets.

114
00:04:04,690 --> 00:04:06,974
Sixth, OpenAI released 722 math manuscripts,

115
00:04:06,994 --> 00:04:09,899
and some in the math community are unhappy.

116
00:04:09,919 --> 00:04:11,187
On October 6, OpenAI

117
00:04:11,207 --> 00:04:13,019
put the batch on GitHub,

118
00:04:13,039 --> 00:04:15,502
produced by an unreleased internal model.

119
00:04:15,522 --> 00:04:17,205
They are grouped into 372 families,

120
00:04:17,225 --> 00:04:19,922
selected from about 4,000 problems posed to the model.

121
00:04:19,942 --> 00:04:21,847
The repository uses the Apache-2.0 license

122
00:04:21,867 --> 00:04:24,420
and holds manuscripts, Lean formalizations

123
00:04:24,440 --> 00:04:26,363
and 10 abridged reasoning summaries.

124
00:04:26,383 --> 00:04:27,963
But not every manuscript has a Lean formalization,

125
00:04:27,983 --> 00:04:29,462
and OpenAI itself warns

126
00:04:29,482 --> 00:04:31,732
that unformalized results could have issues.

127
00:04:31,752 --> 00:04:33,758
On September 29, the Institute for Advanced Study's math

128
00:04:33,778 --> 00:04:34,707
and AI advisory group

129
00:04:34,727 --> 00:04:36,696
published responsible-release recommendations.

130
00:04:36,716 --> 00:04:37,935
It says labs should not treat

131
00:04:37,955 --> 00:04:39,312
result releases as marketing,

132
00:04:39,332 --> 00:04:42,633
and results belong in repositories no AI lab controls.

133
00:04:42,653 --> 00:04:43,510
OpenAI says it is exploring

134
00:04:43,530 --> 00:04:46,435
community-hosted alternatives that meet those guidelines.

135
00:04:46,455 --> 00:04:47,486
Whether the manuscripts hold

136
00:04:47,506 --> 00:04:49,983
up will take mathematicians checking them one by one.

137
00:04:50,183 --> 00:04:51,662
Seventh, the German search

138
00:04:51,682 --> 00:04:53,616
engine Ecosia has dropped Mistral.

139
00:04:53,636 --> 00:04:56,291
According to IT Home on October 8, citing Politico,

140
00:04:56,311 --> 00:04:58,780
Ecosia has switched to Chinese open-source models.

141
00:04:58,800 --> 00:04:59,583
Back in May,

142
00:04:59,603 --> 00:05:02,033
it had just moved from OpenAI to Mistral.

143
00:05:02,053 --> 00:05:04,673
Founder and CEO Christian Kroll said he was disappointed

144
00:05:04,693 --> 00:05:06,561
with Mistral's quality,

145
00:05:06,581 --> 00:05:09,053
calling it a full year behind its competitors.

146
00:05:09,073 --> 00:05:11,373
Ecosia also cited frequent server overload,

147
00:05:11,393 --> 00:05:13,519
and questioned whether Mistral is truly neutral.

148
00:05:13,539 --> 00:05:15,238
It now works with Melious

149
00:05:15,258 --> 00:05:16,485
to use Alibaba's Qwen,

150
00:05:16,505 --> 00:05:19,062
Zhipu's GLM and Moonshot AI's Kimi.

151
00:05:19,082 --> 00:05:21,883
The switch reportedly cut costs in half

152
00:05:21,903 --> 00:05:23,367
and brought performance gains.

153
00:05:23,387 --> 00:05:25,122
The report gives no performance figures,

154
00:05:25,142 --> 00:05:26,599
so one company's view

155
00:05:26,619 --> 00:05:29,200
is not a model ranking.

156
00:05:29,400 --> 00:05:31,920
That's all for today. Sources are in the description.

157
00:05:31,940 --> 00:05:33,393
See you tomorrow.
